+abstract: "An asynchronous, current-mode boost converter with the power switch on the die and the diode outside. It runs from 3 to 30 V and regulates an output from the input voltage up to 33 V, set by two feedback resistors against a 1.24 V reference. The switching frequency is fixed at about 1 MHz, the loop compensation is internal, and a soft start limits the inrush at power-up. The switch current limit is 450 mA minimum, 750 mA typical and 925 mA maximum, so the part suits small loads, such as LED and backlight drivers, with the output current set by the input voltage, the output voltage and the inductor. At light load it switches to a burst mode. EN turns it off to 5 µA typical. The datasheet gives an example of the standard boost circuit at 12 V and one that doubles a Li-Ion input to 50 V with a diode and capacitor charge pump."
